{
  "schemaVersion": 1,
  "id": "dsh-web-without-port-is-named-for-the-port-it-listens-on",
  "title": "dsh web without --port is named for the port it listens on",
  "requirement": "A dsh web started without --port (the composed port) is attributed to the TCP port it actually listens on, read from /proc/net/tcp and the process's own descriptors, so `dsh web --restart` can stop it. A portless process that listens nowhere is machine-wide evidence only and appears in no port's pid list; the check's own process tree is never named; the harness-replacement gate still sees every dsh web on the machine.",
  "kind": "regression",
  "status": "stale",
  "source": "agent",
  "automated": true,
  "testPath": "scripts/test/kit-update-server-scope.test.mjs",
  "runCommand": "node --test scripts/test/kit-update-server-scope.test.mjs",
  "steps": [
    "Start a synthetic dsh web without --port whose bin.js serves HTTP on a free port (SCOPE_LISTEN_PORT).",
    "Run node scripts/kit-update.mjs --check --json --port <that port>: server.pids must name the process.",
    "Run the same check for another free port: that process must not appear.",
    "Start a synthetic dsh web without --port that listens nowhere and check a free port: it must appear in no port list, only in the machine scan.",
    "On this machine: a check run outside the server's process tree names pid 6272 for --port 3080."
  ],
  "expected": "server.pids names the portless server for the port its listening socket is bound to and for no other; a silent portless process stays in the machine scan with port null; the live :3080 server is named for 3080 when the check is not its descendant, and never TERMed.",
  "tags": [
    "kit-update",
    "server-watchdog",
    "proc-scan",
    "portless-server"
  ],
